# Audit results and detailed explanations, part K (q601-q660). Format: see explain_a.py.
E = {}
def e(qid, stem, exp, opts=None, q=None):
    E[qid] = dict(stem=stem, exp=exp, opts=opts, q=q)

e("q601", "An executive summary is written mainly for", "Executives and other busy decision makers often don't have time to read a full report. The executive summary gives them the key findings and recommendations up front, in a page or so, and must make sense on its own. Supporting detail stays in the body and appendices.")
e("q602", "A drawback of purely verbal instructions is that they", "Spoken instructions leave no record, so listeners may forget details or remember them differently. That's why important verbal instructions, like deadlines, numbers and procedures, should be followed up in writing. Verbal messages can include details; they're just harder to retain.")
e("q603", "Effective verbal communication relies on", "Effective speakers use precise, clear words, speak at a moderate pace and match their language to the audience, so listeners understand and remember the message. Heavy jargon confuses non-experts, speaking too fast loses listeners and avoiding eye contact reduces trust.")
e("q604", "Effective communication is best described as", "Communication is a two-way process: a sender shares a message, the receiver interprets it and responds with feedback. It succeeds only when the receiver understands the intended meaning. One-way talking, flooding inboxes or avoiding feedback doesn't ensure understanding.")
e("q605", "In a job interview, which nonverbal behavior communicates", "Appropriate eye contact signals confidence, honesty and interest in the conversation. Looking at the floor suggests nervousness or disinterest, crossed arms look defensive and checking the time suggests you want to leave.")
e("q606", "When creating presentation slides for a client meeting", "Effective slides are simple and organized: short bullet points grouped by topic, clear headings and readable fonts, so the audience can follow while listening to you. Full paragraphs make people read instead of listen, and decorative fonts are hard to read.")
e("q607", "Repeating a company's name and page number at the bottom", "A footer is text, like a company name, slide or page number or date, that automatically appears at the bottom of every slide or page. A header does the same at the top. Pivot tables summarize data, and a macro virus is malware.")
e("q608", "A client complains about a fee. The employee resolving it", "Resolving complaints within company policy is fair to every customer and protects the business. The employee should listen, explain and offer the solutions policy allows, such as a one-time courtesy waiver or a way to avoid the fee. Promising whatever is demanded, or something they can't deliver, causes bigger problems.")
e("q609", "Software that automates sales tasks such as tracking leads", "Sales force automation is a CRM feature that automates sales tasks, such as tracking leads, scheduling follow-ups, logging contacts and forecasting sales, so salespeople spend more time with customers and less on paperwork. Payroll and firewalls serve other purposes.")
e("q610", "Mobile CRM apps on smartphones help financial advisors", "Mobile CRM apps let advisors look up client information and update records right after a meeting, wherever they are. Client data stays current and service stays responsive. They don't replace client conversations or remove the need for data security.")
e("q611", "A shopper buys a more expensive watch than usual", "Situational influences, such as the purpose of the purchase, time pressure and the setting, affect buying behavior. Buying a gift often leads people to spend more than they would on themselves. The store's accounting method and the interest rate don't drive this choice.")
e("q612", "An employee checks in with customers to see whether they need", "Proactively checking in shows customers you care about their needs, which builds relationships and often uncovers needs the company can meet. That helps the company reach its sales and satisfaction goals. It creates value rather than adding cost without benefit.")
e("q613", "The main purpose of feedback from a supervisor is to help", "Feedback tells you what you're doing well and what to improve, so you can grow and do your job better. Constructive feedback is about improvement, not embarrassment or comparison with others.")
e("q614", "When receiving critical feedback, the best first response", "Listening calmly and asking questions to understand the feedback shows maturity and openness, and makes sure you know exactly what to improve. Arguing, getting angry or ignoring it blocks growth and damages your relationship with your supervisor.")
e("q615", "A new employee assumes all older clients dislike technology", "A stereotype is an oversimplified belief that everyone in a group shares the same traits. Many older clients use technology comfortably. Professionals should treat each client as an individual, ask about preferences and set aside assumptions.")
e("q616", "An employee who refuses to try any new procedure and complains", "A positive attitude includes adaptability, being open to change and willing to learn. Refusing every new procedure and constantly complaining shows a negative, inflexible attitude that hurts teamwork and career growth.")
e("q617", "Avoiding situations that trigger impulsive spending", "Stimulus control means changing your environment to remove triggers for unwanted behavior, such as deleting shopping apps, unsubscribing from sale emails or not saving card numbers online. It makes self-control easier because you face fewer temptations.")
e("q618", "Which is a common effect of high stress in the workplace", "Unmanaged workplace stress lowers morale, increases conflict between coworkers and leads to more mistakes, absences and turnover. It can also hurt sleep and health. That's why stress management matters for individuals and organizations.")
e("q619", "A coworker asks you about a client's account balance", "Client information should be shared only with people who need it for legitimate business purposes. A coworker's curiosity isn't a business reason, so you should keep the information confidential. Sharing it violates the client's privacy and possibly privacy laws.")
e("q620", "A company asks employees to sign a nondisclosure agreement", "A nondisclosure agreement (NDA) is a contract in which employees agree not to share the company's confidential or proprietary information, such as trade secrets, client lists and financial data. It protects the company's competitive advantage and clients.")
e("q621", "A personal vision is most useful when it", "A personal vision is a picture of who you want to be and what you want from life. It's most useful when it truly reflects your own values and goals, not a friend's or others' expectations, so it can guide your decisions consistently.")
e("q622", "Having a personal vision helps you", "A personal vision gives you a clear picture of your goals in life, which helps you set specific goals, make choices about school, career and money and stay motivated. It guides planning; it doesn't replace it or remove risk.")
e("q623", "Which habit makes it hardest to manage commitments on time", "Procrastination, putting tasks off until later, leaves too little time to finish, causing rushed work and missed deadlines. Using a calendar, estimating task time and prioritizing all help you meet commitments.")
e("q624", "Before agreeing to a new assignment, a reliable employee", "Reliable people estimate how long a new task will take and check their current workload before committing. That prevents overcommitting and missed deadlines. Saying yes to everything, waiting until the deadline or passing work to coworkers makes you unreliable.")
e("q625", "A manager who encourages employees to use and develop", "Inspiring others means motivating people to grow, use their talents and work toward goals they care about. Encouraging employees to develop their abilities builds engagement and loyalty. Micromanaging controls every detail, which discourages growth.")
e("q626", "Inspired employees are typically", "Inspired employees feel connected to a shared purpose, so they're motivated to take initiative and act toward common goals, often going beyond what's required. They tend to be more productive and open to change.")
e("q627", "Brainstorming in a team meeting is a technique for", "Brainstorming generates as many ideas as possible in a short time, without judging them at first. Withholding criticism encourages creative, unusual ideas, which can be combined and evaluated later. Choosing immediately or criticizing every idea shuts creativity down.")
e("q628", "Taking an interest inventory helps a student", "An interest inventory is a questionnaire that matches your interests to types of work and careers you might enjoy. It helps you explore options and plan education. It can't guarantee a job, set a salary or replace classes.")
e("q629", "Working mainly for a high salary rather than enjoyment", "Extrinsic motivation comes from external rewards like pay, bonuses, grades or praise. Intrinsic motivation comes from enjoying the work itself or finding it meaningful. Most people have both, but intrinsic motivation tends to sustain effort longer.")
e("q630", "On a job application, a question that doesn't apply to you", "Writing 'does not apply' or 'N/A' shows the employer you read and considered every question. A blank space can look like you skipped or overlooked it, and made-up answers are dishonest.")
e("q631", "Information on a job application should be", "A job application should be accurate, complete and consistent with your résumé. Employers compare the two, and differences in dates, titles or details raise doubts about honesty. Applications should be neat and specific, not vague.")
e("q632", "Researching a company before an interview helps you", "Researching the company's products, values, recent news and culture lets you ask thoughtful questions, connect your skills to its needs and show genuine interest. Interviewers notice preparation. It doesn't replace answering questions or preparing your own answers.")
e("q633", "Which resource helps a finance professional stay current", "Trade publications and professional journals cover industry news, regulatory changes, new products and best practices, which helps finance professionals stay current. Examples include American Banker and the Journal of Financial Planning.")
e("q634", "Professional and trade associations often work to", "Professional and trade associations offer training, certifications, conferences and networking, and they advocate for their industry by working to influence legislation and regulation. They don't set members' prices (that could be illegal price-fixing) or replace regulators.")
e("q635", "Assigning a new hire an experienced 'buddy'", "A buddy or mentor helps a new employee learn unwritten rules, answers everyday questions and introduces them to coworkers, so they adjust and become productive faster. It supports, but doesn't replace, formal orientation and training.")
e("q636", "A written description of the skills, education and experience", "A job specification lists the qualifications, including skills, education, experience and certifications, a person needs for a job. A job description lists the job's duties and responsibilities. Employers use both to recruit and screen candidates.")
e("q637", "Which activity best shows entrepreneurship", "Entrepreneurship means identifying an unmet need and taking the risk to create a business that meets it, such as developing and selling a new product. Working for a large company is employment, buying stock is investing and paying bills is routine financial management.")
e("q638", "Why do ethical practices benefit an entrepreneur's business", "Small businesses depend on reputation and trust. Many customers prefer to buy from companies that treat people fairly and act ethically, and word of mouth spreads quickly. Ethical practices also attract and keep good employees. Ethics doesn't make costs zero or replace planning.")
e("q639", "A couple planning to combine their finances should first", "Before combining finances, a couple should openly share and agree on their goals, such as saving for a home, paying off debt or retirement, plus their debts and spending habits. Shared goals prevent conflict and guide joint decisions. Hiding debts or opening many cards causes problems.")
e("q640", "When should you record a debit card purchase or a check", "Record every debit purchase or check as soon as you make it, so your register always shows how much you actually have available. Waiting can lead to overdrafts because pending transactions may not appear in the bank's balance yet.")
e("q641", "When balancing an account, monthly service fees shown", "Bank service fees reduce your balance, so when you balance your account you subtract them from your register, along with any other bank charges, and add any interest earned. Then your register should match the adjusted bank statement.")
e("q642", "An accountant who reports numbers accurately even when", "Objectivity means reporting facts without bias, and integrity means being honest even under pressure. Reporting accurate numbers that displease a manager demonstrates both, which are core values in the AICPA Code of Professional Conduct.")
e("q643", "Small unethical shortcuts that slowly grow into major misconduct", "Incrementalism, the slippery slope, is when small ethical compromises gradually become normal and lead to bigger ones. A small 'temporary' adjustment can grow into fraud, as at WorldCom. Recognizing the first small step is key to stopping it.")
e("q644", "An investor who believes they can't make a mistake", "Overconfidence bias leads people to overestimate their knowledge or ability and underestimate risk, which causes excessive trading, poor diversification and ignored warnings. Loss aversion is feeling losses more strongly than gains, a different bias.")
e("q645", "Recording customers' purchasing habits and payment history", "Customer records showing purchases and payment history help a business understand what customers want, personalize service and marketing, and make sound credit decisions about who can buy on credit and how much. Accurate records reduce errors.")
e("q646", "Which document is usually kept in a customer's file", "An invoice records what was sold, the quantity, price, total owed and payment terms. Businesses keep invoices in customer files to track sales and amounts due. Mission statements, org charts and press releases aren't customer records.")
e("q647", "Studying changes in the economy, laws, technology, society", "Environmental scanning is the ongoing study of external factors, such as economic, political and legal, social, technological and competitive changes, that could create opportunities or threats for a business. Bookkeeping, payroll and inventory counts are internal tasks.")
e("q648", "Why must environmental scanning be done continuously", "The external environment is dynamic: interest rates move, laws change, competitors launch products and customer tastes shift. Information gathered once quickly goes out of date, so businesses must scan continuously to spot new opportunities and threats.")
e("q649", "A bank researching how popular a competitor's new mobile app", "Researching a competitor's new app is scanning the competitive environment, part of the external environment. Knowing what rivals offer and how customers respond helps the bank decide whether to improve its own app or respond in other ways.")
e("q650", "Information systems help managers mainly by", "Information systems collect, store, process and deliver data so managers have timely, accurate information for decisions. They support managers rather than replacing them.")
e("q651", "A system that stores every customer interaction and purchase", "A customer relationship management (CRM) system is an information system that stores customer data, interactions and purchase history so staff can personalize service and spot needs. Payroll systems manage pay, firewalls protect networks and general ledgers record transactions.")
e("q652", "A set of loan amounts is $5,000, $7,000, $7,000", "The median is the middle value of an ordered list. With five values ($5,000, $7,000, $7,000, $9,000, $12,000), the third is $7,000. The mean (average) is $40,000 / 5 = $8,000, a common trap answer. The mode, the most frequent value, is also $7,000.")
e("q653", "Analysts study the spread of investment returns", "Standard deviation measures how widely returns spread around the average. A larger spread means returns swing more, so the investment is more volatile and riskier. Investors use it to compare risk between investments.")
e("q654", "Information management helps a business", "Good information management keeps records organized, secure, accurate and retrievable. That reduces risks like lost data, breaches and bad decisions, and helps the business comply with laws that require keeping and protecting certain records. It can't guarantee profits.")
e("q655", "Which law requires public companies to keep reliable", "The Sarbanes-Oxley Act (2002) requires public companies to keep accurate financial records, maintain internal controls over financial reporting and preserve documents, with penalties for destroying records. The other laws cover pollution, wages and trademarks.")
e("q656", "Using past data to forecast what could happen", "Predictive analysis uses historical data and statistical models to forecast future outcomes, such as which customers might close accounts or how much loan demand to expect. Descriptive analysis summarizes what already happened.")
e("q657", "The first step in developing a project plan is to", "Before buying supplies or assigning tasks, a team must define the project's purpose (why it exists) and scope (what is and isn't included). Every later decision about tasks, budget, schedule and resources depends on that. Unclear scope is a leading cause of project failure.")
e("q658", "A good project plan acts as a", "A project plan is a road map: it lays out tasks, timelines, budgets, responsibilities and milestones so the team knows where it's going and can track progress. It guides teamwork but can't guarantee there will be no problems.")
e("q659", "An employee sees a box blocking a walkway", "The safest action is to remove the hazard right away by picking up the box and putting it away. Slips, trips and falls are among the most common workplace injuries. Stepping over it, leaving it for someone else or waiting to report it leaves the danger in place.")
e("q660", "Following safety precautions at work mainly reduces", "Safety precautions, like keeping walkways clear, using equipment properly and following procedures, reduce the risk of accidents and injuries. That protects employees and lowers costs such as workers' compensation, lost time and lawsuits.")
